{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790015023,"nonce":"ytm+mBVeiauj5Et/mMA6xQtksbk=","title":"No way to see what the game actually draws: an opt-in capture for rendering issues only (the map stays on the data viewers)","message":"Found while testing Prison Standards on the bench, 2026-09-21.\n\n## The picture rule stays\nDESIGN.md (spec 2.5) says: \"no game-side image rendering; a pure function of dump + catalog\". That remains the way to look at the MAP.\n- `map-view` gives ASCII with layers: terrain, things, zones, pawns.\n- `map-dump` gives data planes: terrain, things, zones, rooms, roof, pawns, fog.\n- `rwa render` draws a PNG from the dump, with `--layers`.\n\nThese are keyed to ids, don't depend on the camera or UI state, and are richer than a screenshot for anything about where things are.\n\n## The gap: rendering issues\nSome questions are only answered by the pixels the game draws, and no data channel can show them:\n- a mod's UI: an inspect tab row, a window, a gizmo's look;\n- textures and graphics: missing-texture X, a blank body type, a wrong apparel graphic;\n- overlays and labels.\n\nThere is also no verb that moves the camera or selects anything. Only comments mention `CameraJumper` / `Find.Selector`.\n\nWhat that cost on 2026-09-21:\n- Checking Prison Standards' prisoner-tab row, and its \"Back on plan\" button, meant relaunching with `--xvfb` and clicking through a hand-rolled ctypes/libXtst script. That test found a real bug, git-bug 042d351 in prisonstandards.\n- A `grim` capture of the parked bench grabbed the user's desktop instead. The bench window sits on a hidden workspace, so any desktop screenshot tool is wrong here.\n\n## Ask\nAn opt-in capture that is **only** for rendering questions, e.g. `capture {pawn|thing|at, tab?, window?, out?}`:\n1. jump the camera to the target and select it (`CameraJumper.TryJumpAndSelect`);\n2. optionally open a named inspect tab;\n3. let a frame render;\n4. write a PNG of the game's own frame (Unity `ScreenCapture`, not a desktop grab) into the run directory, and return its path.\n\nNever called by `advance`, the screen, or anything else unasked.\n\n## Acceptance\n- `capture {pawn: \u003cprisoner\u003e, tab: \"Prisoner\"}` returns a PNG path showing that pawn's prisoner tab. It works on the parked bench (hidden workspace) and under `--xvfb`, and never captures the desktop.\n- Nothing in the loop calls it implicitly. The README states when to use it (rendering questions) versus `map-view` / `map-dump` / `rwa render` (everything about the map).\n- Camera position and selection are restored afterwards, or the result says they were not.","files":null}]}